{
  "$comment": [
    "Logical Dag fixtures shared by this SDK's serializer and Python's, in the",
    "spirit of the `test_dags.yaml` that airflow-core/adr/lang-sdk/0004-dag-parsing.md",
    "describes. That cross-SDK harness does not exist in tree yet, so this is a",
    "local stand-in: JSON rather than YAML so both sides read it without a",
    "parser dependency.",
    "",
    "Keys are the serialized-Dag schema's own snake_case names. serialize_python.py",
    "turns them into DAG()/operator kwargs; conformance.test.ts maps them onto the",
    "SDK's camelCase authoring fields through the generated DAG_SCHEMA_FIELDS and",
    "TASK_SCHEMA_FIELDS tables, so neither side hand-maintains a name map.",
    "",
    "Values are plain JSON except the two types JSON has no literal for:",
    "  {\"__datetime\": \"<ISO 8601>\"}  and  {\"__timedelta\": <seconds>}.",
    "",
    "Regenerate the recorded Python output after changing this file:",
    "  uv run --project airflow-core python ts-sdk/tests/conformance/serialize_python.py"
  ],
  "dags": [
    {
      "dag_id": "conformance_minimal",
      "covers": "No schedule and no options: NullTimetable plus the fields Python always emits.",
      "spec": {},
      "tasks": [
        {
          "task_id": "solo",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "dag_id": "conformance_cron",
      "covers": "A cron schedule with every Dag option set, and one fully configured task followed by one left entirely at its schema defaults.",
      "spec": {
        "schedule": "0 3 * * *",
        "description": "a Dag that sets everything",
        "dag_display_name": "Conformance Cron",
        "doc_md": "# notes",
        "tags": ["gamma", "alpha", "gamma"],
        "start_date": {
          "__datetime": "2026-01-01T00:00:00+00:00"
        },
        "end_date": {
          "__datetime": "2026-12-31T23:30:15+00:00"
        },
        "dagrun_timeout": {
          "__timedelta": 300
        },
        "catchup": true,
        "render_template_as_native_obj": true,
        "disable_bundle_versioning": true,
        "is_paused_upon_creation": true,
        "max_active_tasks": 8,
        "max_active_runs": 3,
        "max_consecutive_failed_dag_runs": 2
      },
      "tasks": [
        {
          "task_id": "extract",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {
            "owner": "data-team",
            "start_date": {
              "__datetime": "2026-02-01T00:00:00+00:00"
            },
            "end_date": {
              "__datetime": "2026-11-30T00:00:00+00:00"
            },
            "trigger_rule": "all_done",
            "depends_on_past": true,
            "ignore_first_depends_on_past": true,
            "wait_for_past_depends_before_skipping": true,
            "wait_for_downstream": true,
            "retries": 2,
            "queue": "typescript",
            "pool": "tiny",
            "pool_slots": 2,
            "execution_timeout": {
              "__timedelta": 120
            },
            "retry_delay": {
              "__timedelta": 600
            },
            "retry_exponential_backoff": 2,
            "max_retry_delay": {
              "__timedelta": 900
            },
            "priority_weight": 5,
            "weight_rule": "upstream",
            "executor": "LocalExecutor",
            "do_xcom_push": false,
            "email_on_failure": false,
            "email_on_retry": false,
            "doc_md": "extracts things",
            "map_index_template": "{{ task.task_id }}",
            "max_active_tis_per_dag": 3,
            "max_active_tis_per_dagrun": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "task_id": "transform",
          "upstream": ["extract"],
          "covers": "Every value explicitly at its schema default, so all of them are omitted.",
          "spec": {
            "owner": "airflow",
            "trigger_rule": "all_success",
            "depends_on_past": false,
            "ignore_first_depends_on_past": false,
            "wait_for_past_depends_before_skipping": false,
            "wait_for_downstream": false,
            "retries": 0,
            "queue": "default",
            "pool": "default_pool",
            "pool_slots": 1,
            "retry_delay": {
              "__timedelta": 300
            },
            "retry_exponential_backoff": 0,
            "priority_weight": 1,
            "weight_rule": "downstream",
            "do_xcom_push": true,
            "email_on_failure": true,
            "email_on_retry": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "dag_id": "conformance_once",
      "covers": "The @once preset, fail_fast, and a task feeding two downstreams. fail_fast lives here rather than on conformance_cron because Airflow only allows it on a Dag whose tasks all use the all_success trigger rule.",
      "spec": {
        "schedule": "@once",
        "fail_fast": true
      },
      "tasks": [
        {
          "task_id": "seed",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "beta",
          "upstream": ["seed"],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "alpha",
          "upstream": ["seed"],
          "spec": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "dag_id": "conformance_continuous",
      "covers": "The @continuous preset. Airflow caps a continuous Dag at one active run, so max_active_runs is set rather than left at the default of 16.",
      "spec": {
        "schedule": "@continuous",
        "max_active_runs": 1
      },
      "tasks": [
        {
          "task_id": "watch",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "dag_id": "conformance_diamond",
      "covers": "Fan-out and fan-in, so downstream_task_ids has to be sorted rather than in wiring order. The schedule is spelled out rather than written \"@daily\" because Python expands a preset before serializing it, which serde.test.ts covers separately.",
      "spec": {
        "schedule": "0 0 * * *"
      },
      "tasks": [
        {
          "task_id": "root",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "right",
          "upstream": ["root"],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "left",
          "upstream": ["root"],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "join",
          "upstream": ["right", "left"],
          "spec": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "dag_id": "conformance_groups",
      "covers": "Nested task groups and order-only edges. A group edge is recorded on the group object and also expanded onto the task graph, where it reaches the group's roots and leaves rather than every task it holds -- staging.stage feeds staging.checks.nulls, so only the latter is a leaf. Both sides have to agree on that expansion and on the local _group_id a nested group carries.",
      "spec": {
        "schedule": "@once"
      },
      "groups": ["staging", "staging.checks", "publish"],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "task_id": "extract",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "stage",
          "group": "staging",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "nulls",
          "group": "staging.checks",
          "upstream": ["staging.stage"],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "push",
          "group": "publish",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "load",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {}
        },
        {
          "task_id": "notify",
          "upstream": [],
          "spec": {}
        }
      ],
      "order_edges": [
        ["extract", "staging"],
        ["staging", "publish"],
        ["publish", "load"],
        ["load", "notify"]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
